ata-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Trail.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"102:29\\">Home</a><span data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Trail.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"104:48\\">/</span><a href=\\"/resources/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Trail.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"102:29\\">Resources</a><span data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Trail.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"104:48\\">/</span><a href=\\"/resources/#resources-hub-grid-compare\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Trail.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"102:29\\">Product Comparisons</a><span data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Trail.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"104:48\\">/</span><span aria-current=\\"page\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Trail.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"100:35\\">Google Review NFC Card vs NFC Sticker</span> </nav> <section class=\\"codex-editorial-hero\\" data-page-type=\\"compare\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"115:106\\"> <div class=\\"codex-editorial-hero-copy\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"116:42\\"> <p class=\\"codex-editorial-kicker\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"117:39\\">Review Format Comparison</p> <h1 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"118:9\\">Google Review NFC Card vs NFC Sticker</h1>  <p class=\\"codex-editorial-byline\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"121:41\\">By <a class=\\"codex-byline-name\\" href=\\"/about/review-board/#peter-zhang\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"122:63\\">Peter Zhang</a> · Reviewed by <a class=\\"codex-byline-name\\" href=\\"/about/review-board/#nancy-wu\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"127:67\\">Nancy Wu</a> · Updated <time datetime=\\"2026-07-02\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"132:66\\">Jul 2026</time></p>  <div class=\\"codex-editorial-answer\\" aria-label=\\"Quick answer\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"213:67\\"> <p class=\\"codex-editorial-answer-label\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"214:47\\">Quick answer</p> <p class=\\"codex-editorial-summary\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"215:8\\">Choose the <a href=\\"/solutions/google-review-nfc-card/\\" title=\\"Google review NFC cards\\">Google review NFC card</a> ($1.50-$4) for staff-prompted handoffs and the NFC sticker ($0.20-$0.80) for passive 24/7 placements. Cards hit 30-50% tap-to-review conversion with staff prompting; stickers convert 10-20% of customers who notice and scan. Neither replaces the other: 70%+ of successful local-business review programs deploy both formats in parallel. This guide compares cost, placement, phone behavior, staff training and durability.</p> </div> <ul class=\\"codex-editorial-points\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"217:40\\"> <li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"218:48\\">NFC review card: $1.50-$4 per PVC card, handed to customers at checkout, premium feel, best when staff actively prompts the tap. Typical tap-to-review conversion 30-50% with prompting.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"218:48\\">NFC sticker: $0.20-$0.80 per sticker, applied to counters, menus, bathroom doors, packaging. Passive 24/7 prompt. Works without staff intervention but requires clear call-to-action text.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"218:48\\">Mixed deployment — 70%+ of successful local-business review programs run both formats. Cards capture staff-prompted handoff moments; stickers catch the idle-moment self-service taps.</li> </ul>  <div class=\\"codex-hero-cta\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"222:37\\"> <a class=\\"codex-hero-cta-btn\\" data-cta-tier=\\"hero\\" href=\\"#quick-quote\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"223:84\\">Get a Quick Quote</a>  </div> <div class=\\"codex-hero-trust-bar\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"232:43\\"> <span data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"233:18\\"><strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"233:25\\">Since 2008</strong></span> <span data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"234:18\\"><strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"234:25\\">ISO 9001:2015</strong> sales &amp; service QMS</span> <span data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"235:18\\"><strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialHero.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"235:25\\">Shenzhen</strong> direct supplier</span> </div>  </div> </section>        <section class=\\"codex-editorial-section codex-editorial-snapshot\\" id=\\"at-a-glance\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/DecisionSnapshot.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"42:75\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/DecisionSnapshot.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"43:7\\">At a glance</h2> <p class=\\"codex-editorial-section-intro\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/DecisionSnapshot.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"44:44\\">Use these short answers to decide whether this page matches the project before moving into the detail.</p> <div class=\\"codex-editorial-snapshot-grid\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/DecisionSnapshot.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"45:46\\"> <article class=\\"codex-card codex-editorial-snapshot-card\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/DecisionSnapshot.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"47:65\\"> <p class=\\"codex-editorial-answer-label\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/DecisionSnapshot.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"48:49\\">Next step</p> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/DecisionSnapshot.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"49:12\\">Ready to narrow the options? Start a conversation with the details from this comparison.</p> <a class=\\"codex-editorial-snapshot-link\\" href=\\"/contact/nfc-branding-cards/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/DecisionSnapshot.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"51:74\\">Choose card or sticker</a> </article> </div>  </section>  <nav class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-nav\\" aria-label=\\"On this page\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"20:67\\"><p class=\\"codex-editorial-kicker\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"21:39\\">On this page</p><div class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-links\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"22:45\\"><a class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-link\\" href=\\"#at-a-glance\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:67\\">At a glance</a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-link\\" href=\\"#card-vs-sticker-the-core-behavioral-difference\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:67\\">Card vs sticker — the core behavioral difference</a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-link\\" href=\\"#when-the-card-format-is-the-right-primary-choice\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:67\\">When the card format is the right primary choice</a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-link\\" href=\\"#when-the-sticker-format-is-the-right-primary-choice\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:67\\">When the sticker format is the right primary choice</a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-link\\" href=\\"#combining-cards-and-stickers-the-70-pattern\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:67\\">Combining cards and stickers — the 70% pattern</a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-link\\" href=\\"#sticker-placement-guide-where-they-actually-work\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:67\\">Sticker placement guide — where they actually work</a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-link\\" href=\\"#cost-durability-and-replacement-economics\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:67\\">Cost, durability and replacement economics</a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-link\\" href=\\"#testing-framework-which-format-to-pilot-first\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:67\\">Testing framework — which format to pilot first</a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-link\\" href=\\"#verdict-cards-where-staff-hand-them-over-stickers-where-taps-happen-unsupervised\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:67\\">Verdict: cards where staff hand them over, stickers where taps happen unsupervised</a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-link\\" href=\\"#useful-next-pages\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:67\\">Useful next pages</a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-link\\" href=\\"#faq\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:67\\">FAQ</a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-link\\" href=\\"#sources\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:67\\">Sources</a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-link\\" href=\\"#next-step\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:67\\">Next step</a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-jump-link\\" href=\\"#quick-quote\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/JumpNav.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:67\\">Get a quote</a></div></nav> <section class=\\"codex-editorial-section\\" id=\\"card-vs-sticker-the-core-behavioral-difference\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"75:2\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"76:7\\">Card vs sticker — the core behavioral difference</h2>         <ul class=\\"codex-editorial-list\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"38:38\\"><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Cards live in human hands (they arrive at a customer moment (paying the check, picking up takeout, leaving a salon chair) when a staff member can say &#39;We&#39;d love a quick review) just tap this card with your phone&#39;. The physical handoff creates commitment and reduces friction.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Stickers live on surfaces. Counter edges, menu holders, bathroom mirrors, packaging, window decals. They work without a staff member being involved and catch customers during idle moments (waiting for coffee, glancing while paying, browsing the menu).</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Cards convert 30-50% of engaged customers who tap, when prompted by staff. Stickers convert 10-20% of customers who notice and scan, without any staff prompt.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Staff dependency: card programs collapse without consistent prompting. A location with 3 NFC review cards and no prompting script typically sees under 5 reviews per month incremental. The same location with trained staff prompting the cards hits 25-40 reviews per month.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Sticker placement dependency: stickers in poor locations (under the cash register, behind the coffee machine, above eye level) convert at 3-5%. Stickers at eye level on the customer side of the counter convert at 15-25%.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Carrying behavior: customers often keep the NFC review card as a business contact reference, especially if it doubles as a team member&#39;s contact card. Stickers are one-moment only and do not build ongoing relationship capital.</li></ul>     </section><section class=\\"codex-editorial-section\\" id=\\"when-the-card-format-is-the-right-primary-choice\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"75:2\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"76:7\\">When the card format is the right primary choice</h2>         <ul class=\\"codex-editorial-list\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"38:38\\"><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Staff-mediated service businesses. Salons, spas, barbershops, massage therapy, dental offices, pet grooming. The customer spends 30-90 minutes with a specific staff member who can prompt the review at the personal handoff moment.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Transactional handoff with strong staff rapport. Restaurants with attentive servers, specialty coffee shops with conversation-at-counter culture, independent retail with personal customer service.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Mobile services: home-visit cleaning, in-home fitness training, mobile repair services. Staff hand the card at the end of the service. No fixed surface exists for sticker placement.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">B2B service providers: IT consultants, lawyers, accountants, contractors. Cards carry staff name and double as a leave-behind business artifact with the review prompt baked into the back.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Premium brands emphasizing quality. The metal or wood card signals that the business invests in detail. A $0.30 sticker on a plastic holder contradicts a premium positioning.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Training-intensive teams: cards force a staff conversation about reviews. The prompting script gets practiced. The team builds the muscle of asking for reviews, which compounds over months.</li></ul>     </section><section class=\\"codex-editorial-section\\" id=\\"when-the-sticker-format-is-the-right-primary-choice\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"75:2\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"76:7\\">When the sticker format is the right primary choice</h2>         <ul class=\\"codex-editorial-list\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"38:38\\"><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Self-service and volume businesses. Fast-casual restaurants, self-checkout retail, coffee shops with counter-pickup, unattended kiosks. No staff-handoff moment exists.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Placement-rich environments: tabletop at restaurants (one sticker per table), counter edges, window decals visible while customers wait, menu holders, take-away bag closures. Stickers scale across dozens of surfaces at low cost.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">High-traffic seated venues. Cafes, bars, dining rooms where customers spend 30-90 minutes at a table. A table-edge sticker catches the post-meal review moment without staff involvement.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Packaging and takeaway: sticker inside pizza boxes, on coffee cup sleeves, inside delivery bags. Catches the at-home unboxing or enjoyment moment where staff prompting is physically impossible.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Budget-constrained pilots: at $0.20-$0.80 per sticker versus $1.50-$4 per card, a small business can prototype 50 sticker placements for the cost of 10 cards, learning more about customer behavior faster.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Staff-reluctant teams: if your staff is uncomfortable asking for reviews and training resistance is high, stickers let you run a review program without relying on staff behavior. Conversion is lower but not dependent on prompting.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Multi-location consistency: chain operators can deploy identical sticker placement guidance across 50+ locations. Card programs are harder to standardize because prompting behavior varies by franchise or location.</li></ul>     </section><section class=\\"codex-editorial-section\\" id=\\"combining-cards-and-stickers-the-70-pattern\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"75:2\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"76:7\\">Combining cards and stickers — the 70% pattern</h2>         <ul class=\\"codex-editorial-list\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"38:38\\"><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Survey data across local-business operators using physical review prompts indicates 70%+ of established review programs deploy both cards and stickers simultaneously. Neither format alone captures all customer moments.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Typical deployment — 3-5 NFC cards behind the counter for staff to hand at checkout, 4-8 NFC stickers on tables or menu holders, 1-2 window stickers for exterior visibility. Total program cost $75-$200 per location.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Messaging alignment: both card and sticker land the customer on the same review page (ideally a branded landing page that routes to Google). Consistent branding reinforces recognition.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Analytics split: tap analytics (via short URLs like blp.lk, popl.co or self-hosted URL shorteners) let you see which format drives more taps, which helps refine placement and prompting over time.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Failure recovery: when stickers get stolen, faded or worn, the card program keeps running. When staff forget to prompt, the sticker program keeps running. Redundancy protects the review pipeline.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Segmentation: cards for higher-value customer segments (spa treatment, multi-course dinner), stickers for transactional segments (quick coffee, takeaway). Align the format to the customer&#39;s total engagement level.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Cost scaling: cards replace at 15-25% per year (lost, damaged, handed out and not returned). Stickers replace at 30-60% per year (fade, peel, get cleaned off). Budget accordingly.</li></ul>     </section><section class=\\"codex-editorial-section\\" id=\\"sticker-placement-guide-where-they-actually-work\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"75:2\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"76:7\\">Sticker placement guide — where they actually work</h2>         <ul class=\\"codex-editorial-list\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"38:38\\"><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Counter edge facing customer. The highest-performing position. Eye-level when paying, clearly visible, unobstructed. Must say &#39;Tap here for Google review&#39; clearly.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Table edges or table tents. One sticker per 4-person table for restaurants and cafes. Conversion rises when the sticker is on the corner nearest the customer seating, not center.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Bathroom mirrors or dispensers. Counterintuitive but effective. Customers in the bathroom are at an idle moment and often bored enough to interact with a well-placed sticker.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Window decals: exterior-facing stickers on the customer entry door or large front window. Capture post-visit moments as customers leave. Lower conversion but meaningful impression volume.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Packaging interior: inside takeaway bags, inside delivery boxes, on coffee cup sleeves. Catches at-home unboxing attention when customer mood is often highest.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Avoid: placements above eye level (nobody looks up), on floors or low tables (nobody looks down), behind staff (physically hidden), on moving surfaces like chairs (inconsistent visibility).</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">A/B placement testing. Pick 3-5 placement candidates, deploy 1-2 stickers each, track taps per sticker per week for 3-4 weeks, migrate low-performing placements to the high-performing ones.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Visual clarity: stickers need a dark-on-light or light-on-dark contrast, readable from 2-3 feet, with a clear &#39;Tap here&#39; verb. Ornate branded stickers with faint call-to-action text underperform dramatically.</li></ul>     </section><section class=\\"codex-editorial-section\\" id=\\"cost-durability-and-replacement-economics\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"75:2\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"76:7\\">Cost, durability and replacement economics</h2>         <ul class=\\"codex-editorial-list\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"38:38\\"><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">NFC card cost at 100-500 volume — $1.50-$4 for printed PVC with a clear brand design. Metal cards $12-$25. Wood cards $6-$18. Setup and design $200-$600 one-time.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">NFC sticker cost at 100-1,000 volume — $0.20-$0.80 per sticker with printed artwork. Custom die-cut shapes add $0.10-$0.30. Printed labels with adhesive backing $0.30-$1.50 depending on substrate.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Chip choice: NTAG 213 ($0.05-$0.15) covers both card and sticker use cases for most review programs. Upgrade to NTAG 215 if you want to store both URL and vCard data. Upgrade to NTAG 424 DNA if you need authentication (rare for review programs).</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Durability: a good PVC card survives 2-5 years of light business use. Stickers on indoor counters survive 12-24 months before the printed artwork fades; on windows with sun exposure 6-12 months; in high-wear placements (table edges, pizza boxes) 3-9 months.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">UV-stable stickers: spec UV-stable laminated overlay if sticker placement receives direct sunlight. Costs $0.10-$0.20 more per sticker but triples outdoor life.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Staff-training cost: a 20-minute training session per location costs essentially nothing but 3-5x review volume. The highest-ROI line item in any review program.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Setup effort: card program setup takes 1-2 hours (design, order, program chips, train staff). Sticker program setup takes 2-4 hours (design, order, placement planning, installation). Both are small one-time investments.</li></ul>     </section><section class=\\"codex-editorial-section\\" id=\\"testing-framework-which-format-to-pilot-first\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"75:2\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"76:7\\">Testing framework — which format to pilot first</h2>         <ul class=\\"codex-editorial-list\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"38:38\\"><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Low-budget bootstrapping pilot. Order 10 NFC review cards ($30-$50) and 20 NFC stickers ($10-$20) programmed with the same review URL. Test both in parallel for 4 weeks.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Week 1-2 — observe behavior. Count card handoffs per shift, sticker scans per day, new Google reviews per week. Note which format drives each review via a unique short URL per format.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Week 3-4 — adjust. Move underperforming stickers. Coach staff on card prompting. A/B test different placement texts on stickers (one with &#39;Tap for Google review&#39; and one with &#39;Leave us a review&#39;).</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Decision point at week 4 — whichever format drove more reviews per dollar spent gets scaled first. The underperforming format gets redesigned or deprioritized based on specific findings.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Month 2-3 — scale the winning format, keep the underperforming format on maintenance, track trend. Many programs find the initial winner changes as staff habits evolve.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Customer segment patterns: if the card program dramatically outperforms, your business has strong staff rapport and leans personal. If the sticker program outperforms, your business has strong self-service throughput and leans transactional. Both are valid and should inform future marketing.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Don&#39;t overthink: run the pilot, track the numbers, commit to the top 2-3 placements and the 2-3 staff scripts that work, and iterate monthly. Perfect program design on day 1 is impossible; iteration is where review volume compounds.</li></ul>     </section><section class=\\"codex-editorial-section\\" id=\\"verdict-cards-where-staff-hand-them-over-stickers-where-taps-happen-unsupervised\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"75:2\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/EditorialSection.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"76:7\\">Verdict: cards where staff hand them over, stickers where taps happen unsupervised</h2> <p class=\\"codex-editorial-section-intro\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionIntro.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"19:2\\">Cards ($1.50-$4) convert best in staff-prompted handoffs — checkout counters, table-side close-out — because a human asks. Stickers ($0.20-$0.80) win passive 24/7 placements: counters, menus, bathroom doors, packaging. 70%+ of successful local-business programs run both.</p>        <ul class=\\"codex-editorial-list\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"38:38\\"><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Front-of-house with staff interaction → NFC review card (30-50% tap-to-review conversion).</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Passive always-on surfaces (counter, menu, door, package) → NFC sticker.</li><li data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/SectionList.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"40:10\\">Start with stickers for coverage, add cards where staff can prompt — budget one card per shift leader.</li></ul>     </section> <section class=\\"codex-editorial-section codex-editorial-resource-shell\\" id=\\"useful-next-pages\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceGrid.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"31:81\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceGrid.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"32:7\\">Useful next pages</h2> <p class=\\"codex-editorial-section-intro\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceGrid.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"33:44\\">Use these linked product, guide and comparison pages to keep the next click specific and practical.</p> <div class=\\"codex-editorial-resource-grid\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceGrid.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"34:46\\"> <section class=\\"codex-card codex-editorial-card\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"31:50\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"32:7\\">Review NFC products</h2> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"33:6\\">Cards and stickers designed for Google review programs.</p> <div class=\\"codex-editorial-link-list\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"34:42\\"> <a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/solutions/google-review-nfc-card/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">Google review NFC card</strong>  </a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/products/rfid-labels/ntag213-nfc-sticker/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">NFC stickers</strong>  </a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/solutions/nfc-business-card/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">NFC business card</strong>  </a> </div> </section><section class=\\"codex-card codex-editorial-card\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"31:50\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"32:7\\">Industry solution pages</h2> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"33:6\\">Tailored review-card solutions by business type.</p> <div class=\\"codex-editorial-link-list\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"34:42\\"> <a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/solutions/google-review-nfc-card/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">Google review NFC card solution</strong>  </a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/solutions/google-review-cards-for-restaurants/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">Google review cards for restaurants</strong>  </a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/solutions/google-review-cards-for-salons-and-spas/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">Google review cards for salons and spas</strong>  </a> </div> </section><section class=\\"codex-card codex-editorial-card\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"31:50\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"32:7\\">Related compare pages</h2> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"33:6\\">Continue evaluating format and material choices.</p> <div class=\\"codex-editorial-link-list\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"34:42\\"> <a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/compare/nfc-review-card-vs-qr-review-stand/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">NFC review card vs QR review stand</strong>  </a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/compare/metal-vs-wood-vs-pvc-nfc-business-cards/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">Metal vs wood vs PVC NFC cards</strong>  </a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/compare/rfid-vs-qr-code/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">RFID vs QR code</strong>  </a> </div> </section> </div> </section> <section class=\\"codex-editorial-section\\" id=\\"faq\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:50\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"25:7\\">FAQ</h2> <div class=\\"codex-editorial-faq\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"26:36\\"> <details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">Is an NFC review card always better than a sticker?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">No. Cards work well in staff-mediated service businesses (salons, spas, restaurants with attentive servers) where a specific team member can hand the card at the handoff moment. Stickers outperform in self-service businesses (fast-casual, self-checkout retail, takeaway) where no staff-handoff moment exists, and in placement-rich seated venues (cafes, bars, dining rooms) where multiple surfaces can carry prompts. Many successful programs run both formats in parallel to catch different customer moments.</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">What should a first format test measure?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">Measure four things: actual taps/scans per format (via analytics-capable short URLs), new Google reviews attributable to each format per week, cost per new review, and staff comfort with the prompt script. Don&#39;t measure internal team preference. The data on customer behavior almost always contradicts internal preference. Run the test for at least 3-4 weeks to smooth out day-of-week effects and allow staff to build prompting muscle.</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">Can one chip URL work on both card and sticker?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">Yes: both card and sticker can carry the same NTAG 213 chip programmed with the identical review URL. For analytics purposes, use different short URLs per format (e.g., brand.com/r/card and brand.com/r/sticker) that both redirect to the same Google review destination. This lets you see which format drives more taps without changing the customer-facing destination.</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">How many stickers should a typical cafe deploy?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">A typical single-location cafe benefits from 4-8 NFC stickers. One on each of the main counter customer-facing edges, one per 4-person table (or per table cluster), one in the bathroom area, and one inside takeaway bags. Add 2-3 window decals for exterior visibility. Plus 3-5 NFC cards behind the counter for staff to hand at checkout. Total program cost $75-$150 for the initial deployment plus $30-$80 annual replacement.</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">Do stickers or cards get stolen more often?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">Cards disappear into customer pockets at meaningful rates (maybe 20-30% of cards handed out are kept, which is often a feature rather than a bug. Customers who keep the card may use it later). Stickers disappear from counters at 5-10% per year due to cleaning, accidental peeling or customer curiosity. Plan for both; the replacement cost is modest.</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">What chip should we use for review cards and stickers?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">NTAG 213 is the right default for both. It holds enough memory to encode a Google review URL (typically 60-80 characters), costs $0.05-$0.15 per chip, and works with 100% of NFC-enabled smartphones from iPhone 7 onward and Android 4.0 onward. Upgrade only if you need more than 144 bytes of data on-tag (rare for review programs) or cryptographic authentication (not needed for review URLs).</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">Should the review URL point directly to Google or through a landing page?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">Both approaches work; landing pages convert slightly better. Direct Google URL: simplest, fewest steps, customer lands straight on the review submission. Branded landing page: adds 2-3 seconds but lets you show brand photos, add a &#39;How was your experience&#39; filter (happy customers go to Google, unhappy customers go to private feedback), and capture analytics. For most local businesses, the landing page approach wins on both review volume and star rating because the positive filter protects against unhappy customers leaving public reviews.</p> </details> </div> </section> <section id=\\"sources\\" class=\\"codex-sources\\" aria-labelledby=\\"sources-heading\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Sources.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"60:76\\"><h2 id=\\"sources-heading\\" class=\\"codex-sources-heading\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Sources.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"61:60\\">Sources &amp; references</h2><p class=\\"codex-sources-lead\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Sources.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"62:35\\">Primary standards, OEM datasheets and regulatory documents cited by this article. All URLs were verified on the access date shown below.</p><ol class=\\"codex-sources-list\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Sources.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"63:36\\"><li id=\\"sources-1\\" class=\\"codex-sources-item\\" tabindex=\\"-1\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Sources.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"65:71\\"><span class=\\"codex-sources-num\\" aria-hidden=\\"true\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Sources.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"66:62\\">1.</span><a class=\\"codex-sources-link\\" href=\\"https://nfc-forum.