/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">UHF RFID jewelry tags</strong>  </a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/products/rfid-labels/nfc-gaming-collectible-tag/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">NFC gaming and collectible tags (limited-edition + IP-defended)</strong>  </a> </div> </section><section class=\\"codex-card codex-editorial-card\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"31:50\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"32:7\\">Programs and solutions</h2> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"33:6\\">How the luxury NFC chip connects to your broader brand-protection and DPP program.</p> <div class=\\"codex-editorial-link-list\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"34:42\\"> <a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/solutions/nfc-brand-authentication/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">NFC brand authentication program</strong>  </a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/solutions/nfc-luxury-authentication/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">NFC luxury authentication solution</strong>  </a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/solutions/digital-product-passport/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">Digital Product Passport solution</strong>  </a> </div> </section><section class=\\"codex-card codex-editorial-card\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"31:50\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"32:7\\">Technical deep-dives and related verticals</h2> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"33:6\\">For engineering teams that need the full reference before committing.</p> <div class=\\"codex-editorial-link-list\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"34:42\\"> <a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/guides/ntag424-dna-sun-cmac-authentication/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">NTAG 424 DNA SUN + CMAC guide</strong>  </a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/industries/brand-protection/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">Brand protection industry landing</strong>  </a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/industries/pharmaceutical/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">Pharmaceutical industry (adjacent use cases)</strong>  </a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/solutions/google-review-cards-for-retail-stores/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">Google review NFC cards for retail stores (boutique luxury)</strong>  </a><a class=\\"codex-editorial-link-card\\" href=\\"/blog/luxury-resale-nfc-authentication/\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"36:61\\"> <strong data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/ResourceCard.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"37:17\\">Luxury resale authentication with NFC</strong>  </a> </div> </section> </div> </section> <section class=\\"codex-editorial-section\\" id=\\"faq\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"24:50\\"> <h2 data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"25:7\\">FAQ</h2> <div class=\\"codex-editorial-faq\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"26:36\\"> <details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">How does NFC authentication actually prevent luxury counterfeiting?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">NTAG 424 DNA chips sign every tap with an AES-128 CMAC. The signature includes the chip&#39;s UID, a monotonically increasing tap counter and (on the TT variant) the tamper-loop bit. Your backend re-computes that signature with the card-unique diversified key; a mismatch or a replayed counter fails. The secret key never leaves the chip, so a counterfeiter cannot produce valid signatures even if they record the last tap.</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">Can an NFC tag be embedded in a handbag without affecting the aesthetic?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">Yes. Our luxury inlays are 0.1–0.3 mm thick and can be laminated behind leather linings, inside structural inserts, under watch case backs or inside jewellery clasps. The consumer taps their phone on the general area — no visible tag or marking is required. We always pilot on the actual leather / fabric / casing before a production run because antenna tuning varies with substrate.</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">What does the EU Digital Product Passport mean for luxury textiles and leather goods?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">EU Regulation 2024/1781 (ESPR) makes Digital Product Passports mandatory for categories rolled out from 2026 onward; textiles are on the early wave. A DPP has to carry material composition, supply-chain origin, durability and recycling data in a machine-readable, web-resolvable form. NFC is the most consumer-friendly carrier for luxury because it fits the tap moment the brand already wants. Keep the tap URL shaped as a GS1 Digital Link from day one and your NFC inlay serves authenticity and DPP from one chip.</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">Does the NFC tag enable resale and secondary-market provenance?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">Yes. The chip&#39;s unique ID and tap telemetry are the infrastructure for certified-pre-owned. Your backend records ownership transfer, service events and authentication history keyed to that chip; resale partners verify authenticity with a tap instead of a manual inspection. Some houses publish the trace to a consortium ledger (Aura); others keep it inside their own brand cloud. Either pattern works on the same NTAG 424 DNA chip.</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">What happens if the NFC tag is damaged or removed?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">Damaged inlay = product is treated as non-verified on future taps. Physically removed inlay = the product cannot re-authenticate, which typically disqualifies it from brand service and resale programs. For wine, spirits and closure tags the tamper-loop TT variant treats the break as irreversible — the chip keeps reporting &#39;tampered&#39; even if someone tries to rebuild the trace. Design the product assembly so removing the tag damages the garment or packaging; that is the combined physical + cryptographic deterrent.</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">How does the phone know which URL to open when I tap?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">The tag writes an NDEF record containing the SUN URL. iOS (13+) and Android open NDEF URLs directly in the browser on tap — no app required. Your branded verification page renders on the phone with the &#39;Genuine&#39; / &#39;Tampered&#39; result. Brands that want a native app (for loyalty push, wallet integration, Apple/Google Pay passes) layer the app on top of the same tag; consumers with the app get the native flow, everyone else still gets the browser experience.</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">What is the MOQ and lead time for luxury NFC inlays?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">Typical MOQ is 500 inlays for NTAG 424 DNA TT with custom SUN URL configuration; 15–20 business days, including AES key diversification and tap-counter setup. Plain NTAG 424 DNA inlays run at MOQ 1,000, 15 business days. Bespoke form factors (watch case, wine capsule, sneaker tongue) add 5–10 business days for the first run as we tune the antenna to the chosen substrate.</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">How does Aura Blockchain Consortium use NFC for luxury provenance?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">Aura Blockchain Consortium (founded 2021 by LVMH, Prada, Richemont, joined by OTB, Mercedes-Benz and others) operates a permissioned ledger that records the manufacturing, ownership and service history of luxury items. Member brands typically anchor the chain identifier in an NTAG 424 DNA tap-to-verify NFC tag embedded in the product; the SUN/CMAC signature authenticates the unit, then the brand back-end queries Aura for the provenance trace. ARIANEE provides a similar service for independent maisons on a public consortium. Both architectures work on the same NXP silicon and need no app on the consumer side. See https://auraconsortium.com and https://www.arianee.org.</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">When does the EU Digital Product Passport become mandatory for luxury textiles?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">EU Regulation 2024/1781 (ESPR) replaced the 2009 Ecodesign Directive and introduces the Digital Product Passport (DPP) for product categories defined in delegated acts. The first DPP delegated acts target batteries (already in force under Regulation 2023/1542 from February 2027), textiles and apparel (expected 2026-2027), furniture, tyres and electronics. DPP fields include material composition, repair manual, recycled-content percentage, supply-chain origin and chemical-substance data, served via a unique identifier resolvable per GS1 Digital Link (ISO/IEC 18975). NFC is the dominant proposed carrier for clothing and leather goods because the tap moment already exists. See https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj.</p> </details><details data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"28:16\\"> <summary data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"29:18\\">Can NFC tags survive watch service or handbag refurbishment?</summary> <p data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Faq.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"30:12\\">Yes, with planning. NXP NTAG 424 DNA inlays are 0.1-0.3 mm thick and operate from -25 degC to +85 degC; they survive ultrasonic cleaning baths used in watch service (under 60 degC, neutral pH) and leather conditioning. Tag placement must avoid the bezel removal path and the steam-press zone on handbag refurbishment, which can exceed 110 degC for short periods. Re-pairing the chip to a new service record requires the brand back-end to ingest the post-service tap with a recognised technician credential. Aura, ARIANEE and bespoke brand-cloud architectures all support service-event re-binding without re-issuing the chip. Pilot on each substrate before production.</p> </details> </div> </section> <section id=\\"sources\\" class=\\"codex-sources\\" aria-labelledby=\\"sources-heading\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Sources.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"60:76\\"><h2 id=\\"sources-heading\\" class=\\"codex-sources-heading\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<project-root>/src/components/editorial/Sources.astro\\" data-astro-source-loc=\\"61:60\\">Sources &amp; references</h2><p class=\\"codex-sources-lead\\" data-astro-source-file=\\"<proje